<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I own a RT3S. Apparently, this HT's default value for Step is 2.50 MHz, but I want to make this 12.5 MHz and keep it. On the other hand, OpenGD77 does not seem to have a way to set this value (either individually or globally) so that it can be later saved to a codeplug and written to the HT. Or is there a way? Thanks.</div></blockquote>The VFOs (A/B) each gave their own Step value, which is called "Offset Step" in the CPS, and on the radio this is called "Step" in the Channel Details screen.<br><br>Check out the User Guide<br><br><a href="https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_UserGuide/blob/master/OpenGD77_User_Guide.md#step" class="postlink">https://github.com/LibreDMR/OpenGD77_Us ... de.md#step</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat May 03, 2025 9:20 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
